<p>Well, it has to do with consensus and authority. Anything banking hard enough on either is susceptible &#8212; or at least, that's the simplified version. Money (and commerce more generally) is kind of both &#8212; its value is purely a matter of consensus (i.e. enough people and merchants accepting it in exchange for goods), but of the sort that's infused with authority &#8212; it's backed up by governments, corporations, and militaries (you wouldn't get into the business otherwise) and more often than not, <em>you</em> play by <em>its</em> rules.</p>
